  return <div dangerouslySetInnerHTML={{ __html: "<h1 id=\"getting-started\">Getting started</h1>\n<h2 id=\"requirements\">Requirements</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Python 3.10+</strong></li>\n<li><strong>A Rust toolchain</strong> \u2014 the ledger kernel and vector store are native crates built during install (<a href=\"https://rustup.rs\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer\">rustup.rs</a>)</li>\n<li><strong><a href=\"https://github.com/athena-swarm/athenadb\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer\">AthenaDB</a></strong>, cloned as a sibling directory \u2014\n  the memory layers and the skill library are built on it, so the server does not start\n  without it. <code>install.sh</code> checks for it before doing any work.</li>\n<li><strong>Node.js 18+</strong> \u2014 to build the dashboard. Ubuntu's default <code>nodejs</code> package is older\n  than this; install a current Node with <a href=\"https://github.com/nvm-sh/nvm\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer\">nvm</a> or\n  <a href=\"https://github.com/nodesource/distributions\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer\">NodeSource</a> if the dashboard is skipped.\n  The API and CLI work without it.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"install\">Install</h2>\n<p>Clone both repos side by side, then install from <code>athena</code>:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-bash\">git clone https://github.com/athena-swarm/athenadb\ngit clone https://github.com/athena-swarm/athena &amp;&amp; cd athena\n./install.sh\n</code></pre>\n<p><code>install.sh</code> creates a virtualenv, installs dependencies, builds the native ledger\nkernel with maturin, installs the <code>athena</code> command, and builds the dashboard.</p>\n<p>To check the whole path on a pristine machine \u2014 the exact thing a new user hits \u2014\n<code>scripts/clean_install_test.sh</code> runs it end to end in a clean container and verifies a\nsigned ledger at the other side.</p>\n<h2 id=\"first-run\">First run</h2>\n<pre><code class=\"language-bash\">./venv/bin/athena up          # starts the server \u2192 http://127.0.0.1:8000\n</code></pre>\n<p>Open the dashboard, create an account (the first account is yours), and give it a goal.\nOr stay in the terminal:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-bash\">athena run &quot;explain how a bloom filter works&quot;\nathena chat                    # interactive session\n</code></pre>\n<p>Athena works offline out of the box using the bundled demo backend. For real work,\npoint it at a model:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-bash\">athena models                                   # what's available\nathena models --set ollama:qwen2.5:7b-instruct  # fully local\nathena models --set anthropic                   # needs ANTHROPIC_API_KEY\n</code></pre>\n<h2 id=\"prove-it-worked\">Prove it worked</h2>\n<p>Every step the swarm took was signed. Verify the chain:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-bash\">athena verify\n# \u2713 chain verified   \u00b7   1,382 signed blocks\n</code></pre>\n<h2 id=\"turn-on-the-capabilities-you-want\">Turn on the capabilities you want</h2>\n<p>Athena ships conservative. Enable what you need:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-bash\">athena workspace on     # let agents create real files in a jailed directory\nathena playbooks on     # expose authored playbooks to the swarm\nathena cache on         # semantic answer cache (skips repeat work)\n</code></pre>\n<h2 id=\"useful-next-steps\">Useful next steps</h2>\n<pre><code class=\"language-bash\">athena status           # model, safety, ledger size, capabilities\nathena skills           # what it has learned to do\nathena evolution        # how it has improved its own routing\nathena --help           # everything\n</code></pre>\n<h2 id=\"where-things-live\">Where things live</h2>\n<p>State lives in <code>ATHENA_HOME</code> (default <code>~/.athena</code>): the ledger, memory, skills,\nworkspace, playbooks, and logs. Delete it to start clean.</p>\n<h2 id=\"next\">Next</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"/docs/configuration/\">Configuration</a> \u2014 models, environment variables, capabilities</li>\n<li><a href=\"/docs/cli/\">CLI reference</a> \u2014 every command</li>\n<li><a href=\"/docs/architecture/\">Architecture</a> \u2014 how the swarm actually works</li>\n<li><a href=\"/docs/security/\">Security model</a> \u2014 the sandbox, the jail, and the trade-offs</li>\n</ul>" }} />;
